# Body Shop environment. Copy to `.env` and fill in — `.env` is gitignored.
#
#   cp .env.example .env
#
# Flask's CLI loads `.env` automatically (python-dotenv is a dependency), so
# `python run.py`, `pytest` and `flask --app app upgrade-db` all see these.

# --- Database --------------------------------------------------------------
# Leave DATABASE_URL unset to use a local SQLite file in instance/, which is the
# zero-setup default. Set it to run against Postgres.
#
# Supabase gives you three connection strings under Project Settings → Database.
# Which one you want depends on what is connecting:
#
#   Transaction pooler, port 6543 — the app. Required once Phase 6 puts this in a
#   serverless function, where every invocation would otherwise open its own
#   connection. Server-side prepared statements are disabled automatically
#   (app/db.py passes prepare_threshold=None); it does not support them.
#
#   Session pooler or direct connection, port 5432 — migrations. Run
#   `alembic upgrade head` against this, not the transaction pooler.
#
# The bare `postgres://` scheme Supabase prints is normalised to
# `postgresql+psycopg://` by app/config.py, so paste it as given.

# DATABASE_URL=postgresql://postgres.<project-ref>:<password>@aws-0-<region>.pooler.supabase.com:6543/postgres

# Takes precedence over DATABASE_URL when both are set. Useful for pointing the
# app at one database while DATABASE_URL stays what your host injected.
# BODYSHOP_DATABASE_URL=

# --- Secrets ---------------------------------------------------------------
# Signs session cookies. Production refuses to boot if this is unset or still
# the development default. Generate one with:
#
#   python -c "import secrets; print(secrets.token_urlsafe(48))"
# BODYSHOP_SECRET_KEY=

# --- App -------------------------------------------------------------------
# development | testing | production
# BODYSHOP_CONFIG=development

# ISO weekday the summary week starts on (1 = Monday ... 7 = Sunday).
# BODYSHOP_WEEK_STARTS_ON=1

# Origin serving the exercise photographs. Defaults to jsDelivr at the pinned
# free-exercise-db commit; point it at your own origin to self-host.
# BODYSHOP_EXERCISE_IMAGE_BASE=

# --- Tests -----------------------------------------------------------------
# Unset, the suite uses a fresh SQLite file per test. Set, every test runs
# against this database instead, and the schema is built by `alembic upgrade
# head` so the run also verifies the migration chain. Use the session pooler or
# direct connection (port 5432) — the suite issues DDL and TRUNCATE.
#
# WARNING: the suite truncates workout_entry between tests. Point this at a
# scratch database, never at one holding real workouts.
# BODYSHOP_TEST_DATABASE_URL=
